# Components and React

`"use client"` is the first line of a client file. Keep that file small. Static UI stays in a Server Component.

## Hooks

Rules of Hooks: top level only. Never inside a condition or a loop.

| Hook | Use when | Avoid when |
|---|---|---|
| `useState` | Local UI state | A derived value. Compute it while rendering |
| `useEffect` | Sync with the browser or an external system | A fetch a Server Component can do, or derived state |
| `useRef` | A DOM node, or a mutable value that must not re-render | A value that should update the UI |
| `useId` | Stable accessibility ids for forms and drawers | Keys in a list |
| `useMemo` | An expensive pure calculation, or a stable object or array dependency | Cheap math, or optimization by default |
| `useCallback` | A stable function passed into a memoized child or an effect dependency | Every handler |
| `useReducer` | Multi-field state transitions | A boolean or a string |

Every listener and timer is removed in the `useEffect` cleanup.

```tsx
useEffect(() => {
  const onResize = () => { /* ... */ };
  window.addEventListener("resize", onResize);
  return () => window.removeEventListener("resize", onResize);
}, []);
```

## memo

Memoize a list row that re-renders often with the same props. Pair it with `useCallback` for the handler passed in. Do not memoize the whole tree.

```tsx
const Item = memo(function Item({ label, onSelect }: { label: string; onSelect: () => void }) {
  return <button type="button" onClick={onSelect}>{label}</button>;
});
```

## Forms

Match `app/components/enquiry-form.tsx`: `useForm`, `register`, `handleSubmit`, and `control` for the phone field. Show `formState.errors`.

```tsx
const { register, handleSubmit, formState: { errors } } = useForm<FormInputs>();
```

Client checks are UX only. Real validation is Zod in a Route Handler or server action.

## Data

| Concern | Where it lives |
|---|---|
| Zod | Server. Optional client mirror for instant errors, never instead of the server |
| Page and list data | Async Server Component `fetch`. No SWR on marketing pages |
| SWR or React Query | Only live polling or a cache after a mutation |
| Auth, rate limits, secrets | Server only |

## Dynamic import

`next/dynamic` is for a heavy client-only widget such as pageflip, PDF, or a drawer. Set `ssr: false` when that widget breaks server render.

## Fonts

`SatoshiBold`, `GeistSans`, and `GeistMono` come from `app/constants.ts`. Apply them with `.className` or `.variable`, the same way existing pages do.

## NextUI

NextUI is part of the stack. Use a NextUI component when the screen already uses one, or when it replaces a control you would otherwise build by hand (`Button`, `Input`, `Modal`, `Dropdown`).

Lay the page out with Tailwind. Pass Tailwind through NextUI `className` and `classNames`. Do not add another component library. Do not restyle a NextUI control with a CSS module. A NextUI `Button` does not go inside a `Link`. Navigation stays a `Link`. The NextUI button is for an action.
